atus="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MAGAE, JUNJI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NUCLEAR RECEPTOR RESEARCH LIMITED</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAMURA, GAKUZO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ANDO KUNIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MAGAE JUNJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAMURA GAKUZO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ANDO, KUNIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MAGAE, JUNJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAMURA, GAKUZO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Ligands of nuclear receptors PPAR's (peroxisome proliferator-activated receptors) which are compounds selected from the group consisting of ascofuranone; and ascofuranone homologs and ascochlorin homologs having at least an orcyl aldehyde moiety wherein the hydrogen atom(s) of the hydroxyl group(s) at the 2-position and/or the 4-position of the orcyl aldehyde moiety are substituted by C1-15 alkyl, C1-15 alkenyl, CH2COOH, CH2COO(C1-15 alkyl), C(C=O)(C1-15 alkyl), C(=O)(CH2)1-15COOH, nicotinoyl, isonicotinoyl, etc.  These ligands are usable in preventing and/or treating diabetes; hypertension or cerebrovascular disorders; arteriosclerosis; complications of diabetes; chronic inflammation; cachexia; digestive cancers, etc.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne des ligands de récepteurs nucléaires PPAR (récepteurs activés par le proliférateur des péroxisomes), composés choisis dans le groupe constitué d'ascofuranone. Les homologues d'ascofuranone et les homologues d'ascochlorine ont au moins une fraction d'orcyle aldéhyde où l'(les) atome(s) d'hydrogène du(des) groupe(s) hydroxyle en position 2 et/ou en position 4 de la fraction d'orcyle aldéhyde sont substitués par C1-15 alkyle, C1-15 alcényle, CH2COOH, CH2COO(C1-15 alkyle), C(C=O) (C1-15 alkyle) C(=O) (CH2)1-15COOH, nicotinoyle, isonicotinoyle, etc. Ces ligands servent à prévenir et/ou à traiter le diabète, l'hypertension ou des troubles cérébrovasculaires, l'artériosclérose, des complications diabétiques, l'inflammation chronique, des cancers digestifs, etc.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>